5. Handle all the Next.js Image component props gracefully

This change will allow the TweetPreview component to render properly with Twitter profile images without requiring next.config.js configuration, since we're now using a regular img tag in the preview environment.

The component will maintain its exact appearance and functionality, we're just making it work in the preview environment by bypassing the Next.js Image restrictions. This is a common pattern for preview environments where you can't configure Next.js settings.

